  "title": "Free of Charge Delivery Process Overview",
  "description": "This guide provides an overview of the process for handling free of charge deliveries when a customer does not receive the invoiced quantity of goods. In such cases, a free of charge order must be created using sales order type YVI2 and item category YVF7. It is mandatory to enter an internal reference in this order type. No ATP check is active at the schedule line level, allowing the sales order to proceed without additional checks. Before the picking process, stock must be built up using the NEGO transaction. During the outbound delivery process, the system automatically determines the source of the goods. The outbound delivery order (ODO) is marked, and open delivery items are displayed. The user must double-click the respective delivery item in the header view, select the stock, input the quantity, and save the changes. The subsequent steps follow the standard process, with the only difference being the movement type used. This process ensures that forgotten parts are shipped to the customer efficiently. For more details on the outbound process, refer to the respective video tutorial."
}
