  "title": "Process for Creating Outbound Deliveries in DC",
  "description": "This guide explains the standard process for creating outbound deliveries in DC, focusing on both automated and manual methods. The automated creation of deliveries using transaction VL10 is the recommended standard process. It ensures that items with the same conditions, such as shipping terms and recipients, are grouped and billed together. However, VL10 has stricter rules compared to manual creation, which allows for more flexibility in modifying delivery details before saving. \n\nTo create deliveries automatically, users must open VL10, input criteria like shipping point and due date, and review the prefilled user role (e.g., YVC1). The system generates a list of deliveries due within the selected period, and users can check logs for errors or confirm successful creation. If automated creation fails, manual delivery creation is an alternative. This involves selecting sales orders and items, verifying mandatory fields, and ensuring shipment details like shipping conditions and carrier determination are accurate. \n\nAdditionally, users can verify the creation of outbound delivery orders in EWM and check for any GTS blocks. Both methods—automated and manual—are demonstrated to ensure flexibility and accuracy in the delivery process. The guide concludes with a reminder to review all delivery details, including warehouse tasks and packaging notes, to ensure successful execution."
}
```

