  "description": {
    "overview": "This document provides a detailed guide to the 'Manage Customer Return Order' process (O2C_02.060) under the 'Order to Cash' framework. It outlines standard and special case handling for customer returns, supported by Advanced Returns Management (ARM), and includes tools, transaction codes, and parameters for efficient processing.",
    "key_sections": [
      {
        "title": "General Description",
        "content": "The process handles customer returns for DC materials due to reasons like wrong orders, late deliveries, and recalls, excluding service/repair/guarantee processes and shipping damage claims. ARM is the foundation, covering return order creation, delivery, inspection, follow-up, refund, and billing."
      },
      {
        "title": "Standard Process",
        "content": "The standard process involves creating a return order (VA01) with document type YVH2, entering organizational data, and using return/order reasons for transparency. Approval is managed via the Approval Framework, and the process includes credit memo requests (MSR_CRD), credit notes (VF01), and logistical follow-up actions like goods receipt and inspection."
      },
      {
        "title": "Special Cases",
        "content": [
          "Rejection of return orders or credit memo requests using specific transaction codes (e.g., /SCWM/PRDI, MSR_CRD).",
          "Handling returns for non-migrated R3 sales orders by creating return orders without reference and manually adjusting values.",
          "Managing BOM/KIT returns by canceling price-relevant header items and addressing subitem pricing manually.",
          "Indradrive and Intradrive returns involve unique challenges, such as manual scrapping, separate return POs, and restrictions on resale until the Specialized Fulfillment Scenario (SFS) process is implemented."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Key Tools and Parameters",
