{
  "title": "NSGS Material Handling and Outbound Process Overview",
  "description": "This document provides an overview of the process for handling NSGS (non-standard generic stock) materials, typically identified by material numbers starting with 'BBX'. These materials are not valued or included in inventory counts, requiring sufficient stock availability to be registered in advance. The process begins with the creation of a delivery, which is transferred to EWM (Extended Warehouse Management) to generate an outbound delivery order (ODO) for further processing. Warehouse tasks are automatically created upon saving the ODO. The packing and picking process does not require confirmation for specific handling units and is completed using the STWM-PAC transaction. The SP02 transaction can be used to verify if the printout has been created and assigned correctly. Since the same dummy material can be used for different items, careful handling is necessary. As of May 25, 2025, a new logic is under development to update the weight in the ODO after the packing process is completed. The outbound process after packing aligns with the standard shipping process. For more details on outbound processes, further resources are recommended. Thank you for your attention!"
}
