  "title": "NSGS Material Handling and Outbound Process Overview",
  "description": "This document outlines the process for handling NSGS materials, which are typically identified with a BBX prefix when a Bosch material number is unavailable. These materials require stock to be booked in advance but are excluded from inventory counting. NSGS materials do not have a material availability check activated. The process begins with entering the required information and executing the delivery, which is then handed over to EWM (Extended Warehouse Management). Warehouse orders are created automatically after the Outbound Delivery Order (ODO) is generated. Picking is performed without confirming against a specific handling unit, and the packing process involves creating a new handling unit and assigning the material to it. A pop-up prompts the user to enter the total weight of the delivery item. The process after packing aligns with the standard outbound process, which is covered in other training materials. Note that the logic for certain steps is still under development and will be updated in future versions."
